Q: Invert edge trajectory graphviz A: <p>Main change was to add a <strong>port</strong> position (<a href="https://graphviz.org/docs/attr-types/portPos/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://graphviz.org/docs/attr-types/portPos/</a>) to the head &amp; tail of the edge.  Also removed some unneeded bits.</p>
<pre><code> digraph {
  node[shape=record];
  graph[pencolor=transparent];
  rankdir=LR;

  p1[label=&quot;{&lt;prev&gt;|&lt;data&gt; 12|&lt;next&gt;}&quot;];
  p2[label=&quot;{&lt;prev&gt;|&lt;data&gt; 12|&lt;next&gt;}&quot;];
  p3[label=&quot;{&lt;prev&gt;|&lt;data&gt; 12|&lt;next&gt;}&quot;];

  p1:next -&gt; p2:prev;
  p2:next -&gt; p3:prev;
  p2:prev -&gt; p1:next;
  p3:prev -&gt; p2:next;

  p1:prev:n -&gt; p3:data:n;
//  edge[tailclip=false,dir=&quot;forward&quot; splines=&quot;compound&quot; constraint= &quot;false&quot;];
  p3:next -&gt; p1:prev;    
}
</code></pre>
