<a href="https://i.sstatic.net/LpTtm.png" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/LpTtm.png" alt="enter image description here" /></a></p>

Q: Best practices for using components with a Blazor WebAssembly app if it is ASPNET Core Hosted? A: <p>Necromancer here.</p>
<p>I have this set up and working on .Net10. There's a few requirements in order to achieve.</p>
<p>The API must add razor; map fallback, static, and blazor framework files, etc. It must also define a routes file that contains references to the Client.App file. The API project file must define a <code>&lt;StaticWebAssetBasePath&gt;/&lt;/StaticWebAssetBasePath&gt;</code> and the client project file must define a <code>&lt;StaticWebAssetProjectMode&gt;Default&lt;/StaticWebAssetProjectMode&gt;</code> in a PropertyGroup. There are no changes to the client's start up code, but the API's startup needs to have the following - note that order does matter. The API project also must reference the WASM client.</p>
<p>I have this working with the identity framework as well, so you can know that it's possible.</p>
<pre><code>var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);
...
builder.Services.AddRazorPages();
builder.Services.AddRazorComponents()
    .AddInteractiveWebAssemblyComponents()
    .AddInteractiveServerComponents();
...
var app = builder.Build();
app.UsePathBase(&quot;/&quot;);
// order matters here
app.MapStaticAssets();
app.UseBlazorFrameworkFiles();
app.MapFallbackToFile(&quot;index.html&quot;);
app.UseHttpsRedirection();
app.UseStaticFiles();
app.UseRouting()
    .UseCors()
    .UseAuthentication()
    .UseAuthorization()
    .UseAntiforgery();
app.MapRazorComponents&lt;Project.API.Routes&gt;()
    .AddInteractiveWebAssemblyRenderMode()
    .AddInteractiveServerRenderMode();
</code></pre>
<p>Api/Routes.razor<br />
<code>`</code></p>
<pre><code>@{
    IEnumerable&lt;System.Reflection.Assembly&gt; ComponentDlls = new[] {
        typeof(Project.WASM._Imports).Assembly,
    };
}
&lt;Router AppAssembly=&quot;@typeof(Project.API.Components.Routes).Assembly&quot; AdditionalAssemblies=&quot;@ComponentDlls&quot;&gt;
    &lt;Found Context=&quot;routeData&quot;&gt;
        &lt;RouteView RouteData=&quot;@routeData&quot; DefaultLayout=&quot;@typeof(Project.WASM.Layout.MainLayout)&quot; /&gt;
        &lt;FocusOnNavigate RouteData=&quot;@routeData&quot; Selector=&quot;h1&quot; /&gt;
    &lt;/Found&gt;
    &lt;NotFound&gt;
        &lt;PageTitle&gt;Not found&lt;/PageTitle&gt;
        &lt;LayoutView Layout=&quot;@typeof(Project.WASM.Layout.MainLayout)&quot;&gt;
            &lt;p role=&quot;alert&quot;&gt;Sorry, that doesn't compute.&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;/LayoutView&gt;
    &lt;/NotFound&gt;
&lt;/Router&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>WASM/App.razor<br />
<code>`</code></p>
<pre><code>&lt;CascadingAuthenticationState&gt;
    &lt;Router AppAssembly=&quot;@typeof(App).Assembly&quot; NotFoundPage=&quot;typeof(Pages.NotFound)&quot;&gt;
        &lt;Found Context=&quot;routeData&quot;&gt;
            &lt;AuthorizeRouteView RouteData=&quot;@routeData&quot; DefaultLayout=&quot;@typeof(MainLayout)&quot;&gt;
                &lt;NotAuthorized&gt;
                    &lt;p&gt;You are not authorized to access this resource.&lt;/p&gt;
                &lt;/NotAuthorized&gt;
                &lt;Authorizing&gt;
                    &lt;p&gt;Authentication in progress...&lt;/p&gt;
                &lt;/Authorizing&gt;
            &lt;/AuthorizeRouteView&gt;
            &lt;FocusOnNavigate RouteData=&quot;@routeData&quot; Selector=&quot;h1&quot; /&gt;
        &lt;/Found&gt;
    &lt;/Router&gt;
&lt;/CascadingAuthenticationState&gt;
</code></pre>
